-The six CGOF configurations meet evaluated setup and hold checks (Figure~\ref{fig:cgof-hardware}, Table~\ref{tab:cgof-hardware}). For 1:1, area grows from 106,163.066946 at N4 to 423,513.448454 at N16; corresponding 2:1 areas are 109,794.784709 and 436,771.124393. N16 setup margins are 3.158005 and 1.248813\,ns. At N4, CGOF (2:1) differs from Main by $-0.268019\%$ in whole-design area and adds three registers. Top-level glue contributes part of this small difference. Thus the measured tail benefit is available at a complete cost close to Main under this mapping profile. At the same corner, the representative seed 509/A pair gives 3.416\,mW for 1:1 and 3.462\,mW for 2:1 against 3.466\,mW for Main, while FCFS (3.356\,mW) and RR10 (2.559\,mW) remain lower; these are paired captures, not a mean or significance claim.
